            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Bengali for silt, then the Bengali for to fill in (a pond or low land)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: চূড়া",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "চূড়া — chūṛā — \"a peak; a summit; a top\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "আমরা ভোরে পাহাড়ের চূড়ায় উঠলাম। āmrā bhore pāhāṛer chūṛāy uṭhlām. We climbed to the summit at dawn."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Also the top of anything tall: মন্দিরের চূড়া (chūṛā), the spire of a temple."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "চূড়া (chūṛā) is Sanskrit cūḍā, \"the hair on the top of the head, a crest\" (Monier-Williams); the sense of a mountain top is a natural step, though Monier-Williams gives the head first."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for getting around."
            }
          ]
        },
