              "text": "জঙ্গল — jônggôl — \"a forest; a jungle; overgrown land\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "গ্রামের পিছনে একটা বড় জঙ্গল আছে। grāmer pichhône ekṭā bôṛo jônggôl āchhe. Behind the village there is a big forest."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "বন is a forest in general; জঙ্গল (jônggôl) is wild and thick, and also an overgrown patch of weeds."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "জঙ্গল (jônggôl) is inherited: CDIAL lists Bengali jaṅgal, \"a forest\", under Sanskrit jāṅgala, \"arid, sparsely wooded; a desert region\" (CDIAL 5177); the turn from dry land to thick forest happened in the modern languages, and English jungle is the same word."
            }
          ]
